        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e930b7d3-c621-56ed-9872-8ab94a0fa215",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sly Stone, Mary Ramsey, Moses Tyson Jr.\n- Bands: Sly and the Family Stone\n- Roles: musician, songwriter, record producer, frontman, guitarist\n- Topics: soul, funk, rock, psychedelia, musical collaborations\n\nFacts:\n- Sly Stone was born as Sylvester Stewart on March 15, 1943, in Denton, Texas.\n- Sly Stone is an American musician, songwriter, and record producer.\n- In the 1960s and 1970s, Sly Stone was the frontman for Sly and the Family Stone.\n- Sly and the Family Stone played a critical role in the development of soul, funk, rock, and psychedelia.\n- In 1973, Moses Tyson Jr. started his music career by learning to play the guitar by ear so he could be used on a Sly Stone album.\n- Moses Tyson Jr. is Sly Stone’s cousin.\n- Mary Ramsey has worked with Jackson Browne, Goo Goo Dolls, Billy Bragg, Warren Zevon, Alex Chilton, and Ani DiFranco.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
